{"command":"/home/box/.bun/bin/bun /home/box/.bun/install/global/node_modules/@link-assistant/agent/src/index.js --no-summarize-session --compaction-model same --model formalai/formal-ai --no-retry-on-rate-limits --permission-mode auto --output-format stream-json --compact-json --disable-stdin --no-summarize-session -p Create `tests/unit/issue_936_substitution_compiler.rs` with a red-first regression test for issue #936. Do not edit production code or any other file.\n\nThe test must import this planned public API from `formal_ai`:\n\n- `compile_substitution_rules`\n- `CompiledSubstitutionProgram`\n- `SubstitutionCompilationTarget::{Rust, JavaScript, WebAssembly}`\n- the existing `CrudEvent`, `SubstitutionGraph`, and `SubstitutionRuleSet`\n\nDefine one Links Notation rule set named `counter_loop` with three ordered manual rules. The graph has these links initially:\n\n- `machine:counter -> role:counter`\n- `machine:counter -> control:run`\n- `machine:counter -> state:0`\n\nUse `$machine` conditions and replacements to advance `state:0` to `state:1`, then `state:2`, then `state:3`. The final rule must also replace `control:run` with `control:halt`, so the fixture covers shared variable bindings, conditions, ordered composition, and multiple actions. The interpreted graph must reach the sorted TSV output:\n\n```text\nmachine:counter\\tcontrol:halt\nmachine:counter\\trole:counter\nmachine:counter\\tstate:3\n```\n\nAdd helper functions that:\n\n1. interpret that fixture with `SubstitutionGraph::apply_rules` and render links as sorted TSV;\n2. create a unique temporary directory using only `std`;\n3. write a `CompiledSubstitutionProgram`'s `primary_file` and `supporting_files` into it;\n4. run a child command with piped stdin and return stdout, failing with complete stdout/stderr if the child fails.\n\nAdd one test named `counter_loop_executes_identically_in_rust_javascript_and_webassembly`. It must assert the interpreter applied exactly three rules without hitting the guard. For each target:\n\n- Rust: compile `primary_file.contents` using `rustc --edition=2021 -D warnings`, run the executable with the TSV input, and compare stdout exactly with the interpreted output.\n- JavaScript: run `node` on the emitted primary file and compare stdout exactly.\n- WebAssembly: compile the emitted Rust source with `rustc --edition=2021 -D warnings --target wasm32-unknown-unknown --crate-type cdylib -C panic=abort`, then run the emitted `run_substitution_wasm.mjs` support file with Node and the `.wasm` path, and compare stdout exactly.\n\nAlso assert each artifact's `trace` contains `substitution_compilation`, `verification executable_parity_required`, and the target slug. Keep the file concise and let compilation fail because the planned API does not exist yet.\n","level":"info","message":"Agent started","scriptPath":"/home/box/.bun/install/global/node_modules/@link-assistant/agent/src/index.js","service":"default","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:15:46.804Z","type":"log","version":"0.26.0","workingDirectory":"/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1786841584737"}
